sec-9-name = sec 9

kozhanyy-dnevnik-name = leather diary
kozhanyy-dnevnik-desc = A massive book bound in dark, costly leather, its spine marked with an inventory number in gold stamping. The pages give off a sharp chemical smell of vinegar and burned bone. The author's hand, at first a model of calligraphy, turns by the end into a mad sequence of sweeping scrawls that tear through the paper in places.
kozhanyy-dnevnik-content = [color=#2f4f4f]The Magistrate once again threatens to strip me of funding. Their retrograde thinking is truly [italic]reductio ad absurdum[/italic]. They fear the potential of [italic]synthesis biologica[/italic], turning away in disgust from the idea of merging lifeforms. Oh, [italic]sancta simplicitas[/italic]!


    {"The creation of a speaking chimera is my [italic]opus magnum[/italic]. Common animals reject human ether; their minds are [italic]tabula rasa[/italic], incapable of sustaining a complex thoughtform. Specimens made from vagrants and convicts inevitably collapsed into rotting biomass due to mental rejection. [italic]Ergo[/italic], I required material with perfect compatibility. An unbreakable empathic bond."}


    {"A household dog possesses absolute, unconditional devotion. One's own child possesses a pliant mind, wholly trusting of me."}


    {"[italic]Necessitas non habet legem[/italic]. Necessity knows no law. Science demands sacrifice, and I, as a true creator, am prepared to lay it upon the altar of progress. The seal is drawn with mathematical precision. Transmutation initiated."}


    {"[color=#8b0000]▓▓▓▒▒▒░░[/color]"}


    {"The fusion process is complete [italic]perfecte[/italic]. Bone structures have intertwined into one, ether flows have stabilized. Fur has fallen away in patches, exposing pale flesh, but vital signs are normal. It breathes. It opened its empty eyes."}


    {"It is looking at me."}


    {"[color=#555555]░░▒▓[/color] [italic]\"...c-cold...\"[/italic]"}


    {"It speaks! [italic]Mirabile dictu[/italic]! The vocal apparatus functions!"}


    {"[color=#555555]▒▒▒▓▓▓[/color] [italic]\"...w-why... does it... hurt...\"[/italic] [color=#555555]▓▓▓▒▒░░░[/color]"}


    {"Be silent. Be silent! Your whimpering spoils the purity of the experiment! [italic]Silentium[/italic]!"}

    {"I... I must record the results. My hands are shaking. [italic]Mea culpa...[/italic] What abomination have I made?[/color]"}

potrepannyy-zhurnal-name = battered journal
potrepannyy-zhurnal-desc = A notebook in a cheap leather cover, torn in places, smelling of sour ink dregs and sweat. The text inside is written in the twitchy, bilious hand of a paranoid man, and the pages are often scored with deep marks from the quill.
potrepannyy-zhurnal-content = [head=3][color=#777777]Personal Notes[/color][/head]


    {"[italic]This has gone beyond every limit. Our Collegium is meant to bear the light of science and magic, not become a menagerie for walking corpses. And yet look who now strolls freely through our archives! A walking sack of bones."}


    {"Rosello the Ominous. The mere sight of him is a spit in the face of every decent mage. And our Archmage Vsevolod, having drowned the last scraps of sense in the bottle, allows this filth to meddle with the barrier settings!"}


    {"That bony rogue tells everyone that he lost his flesh in a heroic struggle against the Evil God's spawn while defending our borders alone. What brazen, shameless lies! I can feel it in my gut: something is foul here."}


    {"Every time that creature passes my door, I can feel the stench of dark magic in my very entrails. He does not fight the curse. He bathes in it! I am certain Rosello is a planted agent, a secret lackey of Morbius, waiting only for the moment to bring down the barrier and feed us all to his bony brethren."}


    {"If Vsevolod does not sober up and throw this mistake of nature out the door, we are finished. I shall have to take the initiative and find a way to put this \"hero\" to rest for good.[/italic]"}

zalyapannaya-pivom-tetrad-name = beer-stained notebook
zalyapannaya-pivom-tetrad-desc = A cheap little notebook in a shabby leather binding. The pages stink of sour ale, cheap tobacco, and fish guts, and the letters are crooked, blotted things.
zalyapannaya-pivom-tetrad-content = [head=3][color=#8b4513]Personal Notes[/color][/head]

    {"[italic]Again, curse it, those wolf-bred bastards cleaned out the whole till. Our port slums have rotted through, and the law here is not Therion the Emperor with his legionaries, but that miser Nikolai Kostroving."}


    {"Those legionaries behind their clean walls do not give a damn what happens by the water. And Nikolai, psia krew, has the whole slum by the throat. Today he barged into my tavern with his pack, great boots still caked with mud, squelching on the floor. Sat at the best table, drank a whole keg of good ale, the scoundrels, and tore through a ham in three gulps. And when I, as is proper, timidly asked them to clink some coin, Kostroving fixed those eyes of his on me. One thin look, and my soul went straight to my heels, while my gut knew: say one word out of turn and they would set the place aflame, burning the tavern and me with it."}


    {"The thief drew his cleaver and drove it into the tabletop right before my nose. There, he says, is your protection payment, old fossil. Protection, curse his mother! From whom, if not from him?"}


    {"We live like we are sitting on a powder keg. If no one in the slums turns up to beat Kostroving and his gang bloody and pinch their tails, we will all end up begging in the street, or floating belly-up in the bay.[/italic]"}

nechestivyy-foliant-name = unholy folio
nechestivyy-foliant-content = [color=#aaaaaa]Watching these upright slabs of meat grows more unbearable by the day. Pitiful insects crawling in filth, proudly calling themselves the \"Legion\"... What absurdity.


    {"In their boundless, truly astonishing stupidity, they imagine they can avoid the fate prepared for them. Deny the true faith."}


    {"Lord [bold][color=#8b0000]Morbius[/color][/bold]. Absolute master of death, decay, and the only lawful ruler of this worthless world. How can a herd of mortal worms, whose lives last but a miserable instant, reject the one into whose embrace they will fall regardless?"}


    {"I secretly walked through their so-called cities. They stink of sweat, fear, and living, rotting viscera. Simply standing near them is an insult to my existence. [color=#555555]░░▒▓[/color] Were it not for the great purpose of studying them, I would have wiped these settlements from the face of the earth long ago. They are fit only to become material. Mindless bone puppets in the vanguard of our army."}


    {"But the time draws near. The Gates of the Great Crypt will soon open. We, faithful guardians and servants, already prepare the stage for the triumphal return."}


    {"Let the Legion amuse itself with pitiful illusions of power. When the sky is choked with ash and their own ancestors rise from graves to tear out their throats, these worms will understand their true place. Their worthless lives are only a brief reprieve before eternal service."}


    {"Glory to the Necropolis. Glory to Lord [bold][color=#8b0000]Morbius[/color][/bold]. [color=#555555]▓▓▓▒▒▒░░░...[/color][/color]"}

zamusolennaya-kniga-name = grubby book
zamusolennaya-kniga-desc = The leather binding is worn and stinks of rotten cabbage, cheap tobacco, and sea damp. The pages are smeared with grease, and the columns of numbers are constantly interrupted by crooked notes.
zamusolennaya-kniga-content = [head=3]Diary of Ipat, Honest Merchant[/head]


    {"12th day of Harvest Month."}

    {"Curse this war and every boot in it. The Legion pushes toward the ocean like a blind boar toward a cliff, and the quartermasters, sons of whores, scrape every warehouse clean. \"For the needs of the front, Ipat,\" they say. What am I to them, a milk cow? I gave them a lot of salt beef, the one that had already turned a little lively. Let them choke on it. An honest merchant today gets only a noose and a beggar's sack if he stands around gawping and bowing to every legate."}


    {"15th day of Harvest Month."}

    {"Rumors from the front make the ears wither. They say the rebels have a skeleton running a forge. Roger, they call him. Bony bastard does not eat, does not sleep, just hammers out guns and cannonballs day and night. Our Inquisition is frothing, threatening to burn their fort to the ground for such blasphemy. And I am thinking: I would like loaders like that, curse it all! No soup to cook, no ale to pour, no wages for idle time. Only one problem - if the inquisitors learn what honest Ipat thinks about, they will roast my backside before I can gasp."}


    {"18th day of Harvest Month."}

    {"That wretch Vsevolod Temnov came by today. Eyes flashing, sabre waving - pure forest devil. Lost all fear, the damned deserter! I told him, pay fairly, good sir, and he put a cleaver to my throat. Robbed me bare, curse his mother! Took the best clothes, a sack of hardtack, fresh salt beef, and spat in my face on his way out. Said if I squeak to the patrol, he will come back and hang my liver on the fence. May emptiness take you, villain! Now I sit shaking, hoping the legate never learns where my goods sailed off to. There is honest business for you, curse it by the leg."}


    {"22nd day of Harvest Month."}

    {"The cannons thunder so hard the mugs dance on the table. I hid saffron and the best wine casks in the cellar. If our legate goes completely broke on his damned siege, he will come to wring out the last of my goods. He gets nothing, not my stock. I will bring the quartermaster a slab of lard and pour him a cup, see how matters stand at the front. As they say, the gentle calf suckles two cows, and an honest merchant makes his coin even in war."}

dnevnik-legionera-name = legionary's diary
dnevnik-legionera-desc = A small notebook in a cheap leather binding. The sheets are slightly crumpled. The pages smell of cheap ale and medicinal salves.
dnevnik-legionera-content = [color=#8b5a2b][bold]Third day on guard.[/bold][/color]

    {"Patrolling this cursed trade quarter again. If only someone would steal a sweet roll. The boredom is murderous."}


    {"[color=#8b5a2b][bold]Fifth day.[/bold][/color]"}

    {"Saw another \"adventurer\" today. Had two swords, a heavy crossbow, a staff, and a sack of goblin ears hanging off him, and still skipped about like a feather. Told him not to litter in the square. He looked at me with completely empty eyes, downed ten vials of healing potion in one gulp, and ate a huge wheel of cheese right through the wax rind. Madmen, the lot of them."}


    {"[color=#8b5a2b][bold]Seventh day.[/bold][/color]"}

    {"There was a time when the road of adventure led me too... I went down into the darkest Sewers, cleared caves, searched for secret buttons in stone walls, and hunted foul things. Then one sharp-eyed Lamian shot me in the knee with his [color=#006400]poisoned arrow[/color]. Good thing they are not poisonous themselves, only smear their arrows with filth, or the priests would surely have taken the leg. Now I stand here, freezing in the draft. I shall go warm myself by the brazier.[/color]"}

